---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import EmailSignup from "../components/EmailSignup.astro";
import { DONATION_RAILS, CTA } from "../config";

const showCrypto = DONATION_RAILS.crypto.verified;
---

<Base title="Donate" description="Support independent media: content production, legal defense, and the fight against family court corruption.">
  <span class="pill">Support the network</span>
  <h1>Donate</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every dollar goes somewhere specific. This page lists where, in order — and updates
    when the priorities change.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do with the money</h2>
  <div class="grid cols-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>1. Content</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Priority one, and it isn't close. Documentaries, the daily show, editors, and
        everyone joining the network. Reporting doesn't exist unless someone is paid to
        make it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>2. Legal</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Cover institutions honestly and you get sued, meritorious or not. Legal defense
        is what keeps the reporting on the record — the alternative is quiet retraction.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>3. Fieldwork</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Travel, filming, and time with the people the mainstream won't book. The stories
        that matter rarely come to a studio; the reporting has to go to them.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>4. Reform</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Reporting documents a problem; someone still has to change the policy. Once the
        content operation is stable, contributions above operating cost fund advocates
        working on family-court reform — beginning with Terrence Popp and Second Class
        Citizen, his 501(c)(3) for combat veterans and men inside the system.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="notice" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
    Donations go to JustPearlyThings, LLC. They are not tax-deductible. If a 501(c)(3)
    is incorporated later, its EIN and scope will be posted on this page in writing.
    Until then, treat every contribution as buying reporting — not offsetting income.
  </p>

  <h2>Ways to give</h2>
  <div class="grid cols-2">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Card</h3>
      <p class="muted">One-time or recurring, through The Audacity Network.</p>
      <a class="btn primary" href={DONATION_RAILS.card} rel="noopener">Donate by card</a>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Cash App</h3>
      <p><code>{DONATION_RAILS.cashApp}</code></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Venmo</h3>
      <p><code>{DONATION_RAILS.venmo}</code></p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Crypto</h3>
      {showCrypto ? (
        <ul class="crypto-list">
          {DONATION_RAILS.crypto.addresses.map((c) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{c.coin}</strong>
              <code>{c.address}</code>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      ) : (
        <p class="muted">
          Crypto addresses are being re-verified and will appear here shortly. In the
          meantime, use the address in the description of any recent episode.
        </p>
      )}
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Other ways to support</h2>
  <div class="btn-row">
    <a class="btn" href={CTA.membership.url} rel="noopener">{CTA.membership.label}</a>
    <a class="btn" href={CTA.merch.url} rel="noopener">{CTA.merch.label}</a>
    <a class="btn" href={CTA.gofundme.url} rel="noopener">{CTA.gofundme.label}</a>
  </div>
  <p class="muted">
    Membership is the steadiest support — it's what pays the bills every month. Annual
    plans help the most.
  </p>

  <EmailSignup compact />
</Base>

<style>
  .crypto-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .crypto-list li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }
</style>
